1
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:16,290
Oh, that's right. I understand you
started a family on the other side.

2
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,380
How do you know that?!

3
00:00:19,460 --> 00:00:23,710
I've been curious ever since I heard
about your very lovely daughter.

4
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:27,670
What do you say?
Why not introduce her to my son?

5
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:29,040
I decline.

6
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:33,960
I have His Majesty's word about my reward.

7
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:37,420
Make no contact with the Vankreift family.

8
00:00:39,630 --> 00:00:41,130
I shall withdraw for now.

9
00:00:41,210 --> 00:00:45,670
For now? You mean from now on, Your Highness.

10
00:00:51,170 --> 00:00:52,250
Come in.

11
00:00:55,330 --> 00:00:57,540
Welcome home, Lord Rovel.

12
00:00:57,630 --> 00:01:02,040
Lord Sauvel returned earlier,
saying today was to be celebrated...

13
00:01:02,130 --> 00:01:03,170
Alberto!

14
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:04,790
Yes, my lord?

15
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:10,330
Whether you acted for the good of this family
or not, do not anger me any further.

16
00:01:11,670 --> 00:01:13,920
I'm relieving you as Sauvel's bodyguard.

17
00:01:15,830 --> 00:01:17,420
Consider yourself suspended.

18
00:01:18,830 --> 00:01:20,210
As you wish.

19
00:02:56,130 --> 00:03:00,080
KING RAVISEL

20
00:03:02,380 --> 00:03:04,500
Oh, how could this...

21
00:03:04,750 --> 00:03:07,250
Rovel. It really is you, isn't it?

22
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,170
Mother.

23
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:15,080
Oh, I'm so glad you're safe...

24
00:03:16,130 --> 00:03:18,880
I'm terribly sorry to have
been away for so long.

25
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:20,960
It's you that we're talking about, after all.

26
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:23,710
We were saying perhaps
you weren't coming home

27
00:03:23,790 --> 00:03:26,500
out of adamant refusal to marry that woman.

28
00:03:26,580 --> 00:03:29,250
You saw right through me. My goodness.

29
00:03:29,540 --> 00:03:33,580
And yet, I never imagined
she'd marry Sauvel...

30
00:03:34,290 --> 00:03:37,080
But it seems you've chased her away.

31
00:03:37,170 --> 00:03:38,250
Yes.

32
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:42,290
Roren, be sure to send all of that
woman's belongings to the castle tomorrow.

33
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:43,920
It would be my pleasure.

34
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:46,380
By the way, where is Alberto?

35
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:48,830
On that matter...

36
00:03:50,130 --> 00:03:51,420
I relieved him of his duties

37
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:53,080
and placed him under suspension for now.

38
00:03:53,170 --> 00:03:54,170
What?

39
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:58,000
It seems he has a rather loose tongue.
He's not to be trusted.

40
00:03:59,170 --> 00:04:02,000
What do you mean? Please explain.

41
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:07,250
In truth, I am already married.
I have a spirit wife and a child.

42
00:04:07,330 --> 00:04:08,330
What?

43
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:11,750
This is something only a select few know.

44
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:18,880
However, Prince Ravisel has asked
to introduce his son and my daughter.

45
00:04:19,210 --> 00:04:22,750
And you suspect Alberto
of telling His Highness?

46
00:04:22,830 --> 00:04:28,420
Indeed. The royal family bears a curse
that prevents them from contacting spirits.

47
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:32,420
And the irritating part is that
His Highness likely intends

48
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:34,960
to use my daughter to solve that problem.

49
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:38,460
Are you saying Alberto was using
Lady Ellen as a bargaining chip?

50
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:39,500
That's right.

51
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:41,420
What treachery!

52
00:04:42,330 --> 00:04:43,880
Shall I finish him off?

53
00:04:44,830 --> 00:04:46,170
There's no need for that.

54
00:04:46,250 --> 00:04:48,330
It would fly in the face
of my father's feelings.

55
00:04:49,670 --> 00:04:52,460
Alberto felt indebted to Father.

56
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:56,460
He may have been trying to seek the royal
family's intentions regarding Agiel.

57
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:58,330
Apologies, my brother.

58
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:01,670
This is all because of how pathetic I was.

59
00:05:01,750 --> 00:05:02,710
That's enough.

60
00:05:02,790 --> 00:05:06,540
Well, I'll need to be cautious,
but on the positive side,

61
00:05:06,630 --> 00:05:09,750
I can now introduce my wife
and daughter to society.

62
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:12,460
Rovel, are you not forgetting something?

63
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:13,960
Yes?

64
00:05:14,170 --> 00:05:19,380
Shouldn't you introduce
your wife and daughter to <i>me</i> first?

65
00:05:20,830 --> 00:05:22,330
My, my.

66
00:05:23,170 --> 00:05:25,710
Mother, are you not scared?

67
00:05:25,790 --> 00:05:26,750
Of what?

68
00:05:26,830 --> 00:05:31,960
Of Father's mother!
That makes her your mother-in-law!

69
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:37,250
Gosh, you've already learned that
word too, Ellen? Good job!

70
00:05:37,330 --> 00:05:42,080
That's not what this is about!
What are you going to do if she's scary?

71
00:05:42,170 --> 00:05:46,710
It'll be fine. If things gets awkward,
we'll just never see each other again.

72
00:05:46,790 --> 00:05:51,750
You're taking this so lightly...
But that's just like you, Mother.

73
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:56,210
So, when will you allow me to meet them?

74
00:05:56,290 --> 00:05:58,500
Er, I'm on it.

75
00:05:58,580 --> 00:06:00,000
Ori, Ellen!

76
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:05,670
Darling!

77
00:06:07,750 --> 00:06:09,830
Father, you did a great job!

78
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,880
Oh, Ellen!

79
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:13,500
My, my, my!

80
00:06:14,630 --> 00:06:20,750
Mother, let me introduce you
to my wife, Ori, and my daughter, Ellen.

81
00:06:21,170 --> 00:06:23,670
Could it be? Is this woman your spirit?

82
00:06:23,750 --> 00:06:26,630
Indeed, she is the spirit queen.

83
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,630
It's been a while.

84
00:06:28,710 --> 00:06:34,290
In this world, I'm known by such names as
the Primordial King or Mother of All Things.

85
00:06:34,380 --> 00:06:35,830
My heavens...

86
00:06:36,250 --> 00:06:40,710
Your granddaughter will be the
next queen of the spirit world.

87
00:06:40,790 --> 00:06:43,790
Please regard the two of us with open arms.

88
00:06:47,210 --> 00:06:48,790
Go on, Ellen.

89
00:06:53,540 --> 00:06:55,920
Nice to meet you. I'm Ellen.

90
00:06:57,130 --> 00:07:00,790
To think my granddaughter is going
to be the future spirit queen...

91
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:02,880
How wonderful!

92
00:07:04,250 --> 00:07:06,330
Will you call me grandma?

93
00:07:06,630 --> 00:07:07,670
Huh?

94
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:10,500
<i>Is it really okay</i>
<i>to get all familiar like that?</i>

95
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:12,960
<i>Maybe "Grandmother" would feel less rude?</i>

96
00:07:13,670 --> 00:07:18,420
Gra... Gra... Gra...

97
00:07:19,210 --> 00:07:21,080
Grammie!

98
00:07:22,420 --> 00:07:23,540
Did you hear that?!

99
00:07:23,630 --> 00:07:25,080
Hey, did you catch that?!

100
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:28,460
My goodness, how adorable!

101
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:33,210
Truly, isn't she?! Lady Ellen is
such a splendid, precious child!

102
00:07:33,290 --> 00:07:34,710
Pawpaw...

103
00:07:34,790 --> 00:07:39,130
Oh? Roren, you're having her call you pawpaw?

104
00:07:39,210 --> 00:07:40,790
You've got good taste.

105
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:42,420
Precisely, milady!

106
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:47,080
When Lady Ellen calls me that,
I feel so young again!

107
00:07:47,170 --> 00:07:49,130
Ellen's rather popular.

108
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:54,960
Here, help yourself.

109
00:07:55,210 --> 00:07:57,670
<i>Dessert! I'm so excited!</i>

110
00:07:58,710 --> 00:08:04,080
<i>Wait... They might still be testing me.</i>

111
00:08:04,170 --> 00:08:07,580
My, you've gotten all quiet.
What's the matter?

112
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:09,500
Here, have some.

113
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:17,420
Most impressive. Is dining etiquette
the same in the spirit world?

114
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:21,670
No, seeing as we spirits rarely eat.

115
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:23,670
Did you teach her table manners, dear?

116
00:08:23,750 --> 00:08:25,830
No, I didn't teach her a thing.

117
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:32,170
My, even the way she eats is so adorable!

118
00:08:33,130 --> 00:08:34,630
Ellen.

119
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:36,500
Here. Say, "Ah!"

120
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:37,540
Ah!

121
00:08:37,630 --> 00:08:42,380
Mother! Feeding her is all well and good,
but at this rate, you'll spoil her dinner.

122
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:44,040
Oh dear.

123
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:47,040
My, I'm sorry, Ellen.

124
00:08:47,130 --> 00:08:50,330
But she looks just precious
even when she's disappointed!

125
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:57,290
Sauvel, about moving forward...
Shall I assist you on the business side?

126
00:08:57,380 --> 00:09:00,210
If possible, I would like to refrain
from joining the knights.

127
00:09:00,290 --> 00:09:02,460
You're truly going to assist me?

128
00:09:02,710 --> 00:09:08,080
Yes. Although I won't be able to live here,
since I have Ori and Ellen.

129
00:09:08,170 --> 00:09:10,130
Oh, is that so?

130
00:09:10,330 --> 00:09:15,290
My powers are too great to stay here.
They would affect the human world.

131
00:09:15,670 --> 00:09:20,420
My power of harvest could easily
turn this area into a forest.

132
00:09:20,500 --> 00:09:21,960
My!

133
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:26,880
And what kind of spirit are you, Ellen?
A flower perhaps?

134
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:29,540
It's okay.

135
00:09:31,670 --> 00:09:36,420
I can control... elements.

136
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:38,130
Elements?

137
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:42,540
Um... Elements are
the building blocks of matter.

138
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:45,290
There are countless combinations of them,

139
00:09:45,380 --> 00:09:49,290
and most substances are made up
of said combinations.

140
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:50,330
HUH?

141
00:09:50,420 --> 00:09:53,790
<i>Oh, shoot! How should I explain this?</i>

142
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:57,960
Do you see this? It's charcoal.

143
00:09:58,460 --> 00:10:02,500
But if I use my powers to change
its crystal structure...

144
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:05,710
Here we are!

145
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:10,290
Oh, that's a diamond just like my ring.

146
00:10:10,380 --> 00:10:11,540
That's right!

147
00:10:12,830 --> 00:10:15,960
Charcoal turned into something this beautiful?

148
00:10:16,420 --> 00:10:19,380
To be honest, I don't understand it myself.

149
00:10:19,460 --> 00:10:23,500
It's difficult to explain spirit
powers to humans, isn't it?

150
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:26,750
Does that mean you can
freely produce minerals?

151
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:28,380
I can!

152
00:10:31,920 --> 00:10:33,960
Here, some gold.

153
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,580
Brother, this is...

154
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:39,880
What do you think?

155
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,330
You can sell it if you want.

156
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:43,170
We mustn't, Ellen.

157
00:10:43,250 --> 00:10:47,830
There'd be a huge uproar if we put
something so rare out into the world.

158
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:51,210
Then we should just do this.

159
00:10:52,630 --> 00:10:54,580
Here you go. For you, Grammie.

160
00:10:54,830 --> 00:10:55,790
My!

161
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:56,830
Goodness...

162
00:10:56,920 --> 00:11:00,750
Hey, Ellen, what are you going
to do with that mountain of gold?

163
00:11:00,830 --> 00:11:01,790
Oh...

164
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:03,670
You're making too much, sweetie.

165
00:11:03,750 --> 00:11:05,540
I'll be careful from now on.

166
00:11:06,290 --> 00:11:08,250
To make up for Agiel's squandering,

167
00:11:08,750 --> 00:11:11,380
use this toward public funds
to benefit the citizens.

168
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:12,580
It's yours.

169
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:16,250
Then that's what I shall do.

170
00:11:16,750 --> 00:11:19,670
Oh, but it could put the marketplace in turmoil,

171
00:11:19,750 --> 00:11:24,210
so it may be better to mix
in some impurities before selling it.

172
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:26,880
Lady Ellen, are you certain
you're all right with this?

173
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:30,130
I am. Please buy me cake again!

174
00:11:30,210 --> 00:11:35,460
Most certainly! I could probably
buy one the size of this mansion.

175
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:38,580
Ellen's powers are truly something.

176
00:11:38,670 --> 00:11:43,250
Right? Which is why we can't let the
royal family find out about them.

177
00:11:43,330 --> 00:11:46,250
Yes. No one is to breathe a word of this.

178
00:11:46,330 --> 00:11:50,290
And if we are to sell the gold,
we must prepare an origin for it.

179
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:53,670
Do you own a mine somewhere?

180
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:56,500
I can make it so that it can
be excavated from there.

181
00:11:57,960 --> 00:12:00,750
Huh? Did I say something I shouldn't have?

182
00:12:02,250 --> 00:12:04,460
What a clever child.

183
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:07,670
Speaking of mines, I believe
we have a small one.

184
00:12:07,750 --> 00:12:12,920
In that case, I'll include things mined
there to avoid suspicion.

185
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:17,130
Amazing! She's spouting ideas
that would put adults to shame.

186
00:12:17,210 --> 00:12:19,000
<i>I am an adult on the inside, after all.</i>

187
00:12:19,710 --> 00:12:23,920
If there's anything I can help with on the
business side, please do let me know.

188
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,170
Hold it right there, Miss Ellen...

189
00:12:30,420 --> 00:12:31,670
Everyone, listen up!

190
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
Agiel has returned to the royal family.

191
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:36,210
Well done tolerating her all this time!

192
00:12:38,830 --> 00:12:43,170
As you can see, not only has my older brother
come back to us, but our family has grown.

193
00:12:43,250 --> 00:12:44,790
A joyous occasion indeed.

194
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:48,880
So tonight, although small,
we've decided to throw this party.

195
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:56,960
Everyone, I'm sorry it took this long.
Also, thank you for the preparations tonight.

196
00:12:57,040 --> 00:13:01,790
Now, everyone, drink up
and enjoy yourselves. Cheers!

197
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:03,460
Cheers!

198
00:13:19,630 --> 00:13:23,330
Lady Ellen, would you like more juice?

199
00:13:24,330 --> 00:13:26,170
Pawpaw, this is delicious!

200
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:30,170
I will have to compliment the chef.

201
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:31,920
Yes, I see.

202
00:13:32,460 --> 00:13:34,830
Pawpaw? What are you doing?

203
00:13:35,460 --> 00:13:39,790
For the future, I'm keeping record
of all of your favorite things.

204
00:13:41,210 --> 00:13:43,000
Thank you, Pawpaw!

205
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:47,750
Roren, your expressions are losing their edge.

206
00:13:47,830 --> 00:13:49,880
Most certainly, Your Grace.

207
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:55,380
It is rare to find someone
so worth fawning over.

208
00:13:55,830 --> 00:13:57,710
I am itching to show my skills!

209
00:13:57,790 --> 00:13:59,790
My, Roren.

210
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:03,540
Ellen must truly understand
the hearts of our servants.

211
00:14:03,630 --> 00:14:04,830
You're so clever.

212
00:14:06,290 --> 00:14:08,040
You're going to stop reporting to me?

213
00:14:08,540 --> 00:14:09,500
Yes.

214
00:14:09,580 --> 00:14:13,830
Lord Rovel caught on and dismissed me
from Lord Sauvel's side.

215
00:14:14,130 --> 00:14:18,790
Oh, I see. That was quick.
I'd expect no less of Rovel.

216
00:14:20,670 --> 00:14:22,630
Did you speak to the daughter?

217
00:14:23,130 --> 00:14:24,130
Yes.

218
00:14:24,210 --> 00:14:25,460
Perfect.

219
00:14:26,540 --> 00:14:29,920
Then could you do one last job for me?

220
00:14:34,210 --> 00:14:37,630
Sauvel, that was a wonderful party.

221
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:40,750
I'm pleased to hear you say so, Mother.

222
00:14:42,710 --> 00:14:46,880
Now then, I think it's best we start
heading back to the spirit world.

223
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:47,920
Yes.

224
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:48,960
- What?
- My word!

225
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:50,130
- Already?
- You're going already?

226
00:14:50,210 --> 00:14:53,790
Are you certain you want a forest in your yard?

227
00:14:58,290 --> 00:14:59,330
What about Ellen?

228
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:01,330
Yes, what about Lady Ellen?

229
00:15:03,460 --> 00:15:07,040
Well, Ellen doesn't have
that sort of power, right?

230
00:15:07,130 --> 00:15:08,210
That's right.

231
00:15:08,460 --> 00:15:11,750
Then let's have you sleep over tonight!

232
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:14,630
A sleepover?

233
00:15:14,710 --> 00:15:19,670
Yeah. It might be good to enjoy the
human world once in a while, Ellen.

234
00:15:20,630 --> 00:15:24,420
It seems Father wants some alone
time with Mother, so that's what I'll do.

235
00:15:24,670 --> 00:15:25,920
Oh dear.

236
00:15:26,170 --> 00:15:28,540
There should be a limit to your cleverness.

237
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:31,040
<i>I got the hint.</i>

238
00:15:31,130 --> 00:15:33,630
We'll come in the morning, okay?

239
00:15:33,710 --> 00:15:36,080
Be a good girl, Ellen.

240
00:15:42,540 --> 00:15:45,130
You're tired, aren't you, Ellen?

241
00:15:45,670 --> 00:15:48,170
Do you want to go sleepy-bye with Grammie?

242
00:15:48,250 --> 00:15:49,210
Okie.

243
00:15:49,290 --> 00:15:52,170
I will have your rooms ready right away.

244
00:15:52,250 --> 00:15:54,580
You go on to bed.

245
00:15:54,670 --> 00:15:58,750
Grammie is going to take a bath,
so lie down and rest.

246
00:15:59,670 --> 00:16:00,710
Okie.

247
00:16:09,750 --> 00:16:13,290
Lady Ellen, please wake up. Lady Ellen.

248
00:16:19,830 --> 00:16:22,670
Uncle Alberto?

249
00:16:23,880 --> 00:16:24,920
Take this.

250
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:29,790
For me?

251
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:33,330
Oh, it's from Mr. Blackheart...

252
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:35,960
Prince Ravisel.

253
00:16:38,790 --> 00:16:43,170
The royal family bears a curse
that prevents them from contacting spirits.

254
00:16:43,250 --> 00:16:47,130
And the irritating part is that
His Highness likely intends

255
00:16:47,210 --> 00:16:49,750
to use my daughter to solve that problem.

256
00:16:51,960 --> 00:16:55,420
Do you hate my family, Uncle?

257
00:16:56,170 --> 00:16:57,920
Of course I don't!

258
00:17:02,250 --> 00:17:04,960
Pardon my rudeness.

259
00:17:05,790 --> 00:17:08,250
My father is very angry with you.

260
00:17:08,790 --> 00:17:10,040
I am aware.

261
00:17:11,580 --> 00:17:15,170
I think what you did
with good intentions was

262
00:17:15,540 --> 00:17:19,750
something my father and the others consider
to be unwelcome interference.

263
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:25,380
My father and I are both
half-human and half-spirit.

264
00:17:25,790 --> 00:17:28,960
In the royal family's eyes,
that makes us valuable assets.

265
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:33,750
However, in our eyes, it's a big nuisance.

266
00:17:35,630 --> 00:17:36,960
Why is that?

267
00:17:37,330 --> 00:17:40,750
Since the royal family remains
completely unaware of their faults,

268
00:17:40,830 --> 00:17:42,830
this cursed cycle will never end...

269
00:17:45,630 --> 00:17:47,960
They've forgotten they
incurred the spirits' wrath,

270
00:17:48,080 --> 00:17:50,630
and even the reason behind it...

271
00:17:51,130 --> 00:17:53,130
That arrogance speaks for itself.

272
00:17:55,380 --> 00:17:58,290
Is this invite from him personally?

273
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:03,880
Uncle, immediately cut ties with His Highness.

274
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:07,670
If Father finds out about this,
he'll surely punish you.

275
00:18:09,210 --> 00:18:11,210
I'm aware of that.

276
00:18:11,580 --> 00:18:15,540
It's obvious that His Highness
doesn't care for you one bit, Uncle.

277
00:18:15,630 --> 00:18:21,960
That blackhearted man won't care
if my family turns you away.

278
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:28,000
If you feel indebted to this family,
reevaluate what's really important.

279
00:18:29,250 --> 00:18:32,210
My apologies, Lady Ellen...

280
00:18:32,750 --> 00:18:36,670
That said, I think Father has probably
already picked up on the situation

281
00:18:36,750 --> 00:18:38,790
and is watching from somewhere as we speak.

282
00:18:40,460 --> 00:18:42,750
I'll persuade him.

283
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:49,080
Also, please tell Mr. Blackheart that I must
decline so as not to anger my father.

284
00:18:49,170 --> 00:18:50,250
Yes, milady.

285
00:18:53,250 --> 00:18:55,250
Well then, good night.

286
00:19:00,290 --> 00:19:01,670
Good morning.

287
00:19:01,750 --> 00:19:04,290
Grammie, good morning!

288
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:08,540
My goodness! You truly are adorable!

289
00:19:08,630 --> 00:19:12,170
Lady Isabella, you are
going to crush Lady Ellen.

290
00:19:13,580 --> 00:19:14,920
Here you go.

291
00:19:15,250 --> 00:19:17,000
Pawpaw, thank you!

292
00:19:20,710 --> 00:19:22,920
So adorable!

293
00:19:25,330 --> 00:19:26,880
Morning, Ellen.

294
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:31,880
Father, good morning. Did you get
to have some lovely alone time with Mother?

295
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:33,670
Of course I did...

296
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:35,710
Wait, not that!

297
00:19:36,250 --> 00:19:39,790
Ellen, don't you have something else
to say to your father?

298
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:41,250
Yes.

299
00:19:41,330 --> 00:19:46,880
Uncle Alberto has cut ties with His Highness,
so I ask that you lift his suspension.

300
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:48,330
Ellen!

301
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:56,630
Father, don't <i>you</i> have
something to say to <i>me</i>?

302
00:19:58,250 --> 00:19:59,500
What is this about?

303
00:20:01,290 --> 00:20:05,750
Father was convinced that a messenger
from the prince would come see me,

304
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:08,540
so he deliberately had me
stay here alone last night.

305
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:11,500
Explain yourself, Rovel.

306
00:20:14,420 --> 00:20:16,000
He's just being overprotective.

307
00:20:16,460 --> 00:20:21,960
Now that His Highness knows of my existence,
there's no way he'll leave me be.

308
00:20:23,540 --> 00:20:25,630
I think you're already aware,

309
00:20:25,710 --> 00:20:28,750
but I burned the prince's letter
without reading it.

310
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:32,960
What? You burned a letter
from the prince without reading it?

311
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:34,500
What is this about?

312
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:36,710
This was a way of getting back at Father.

313
00:20:37,130 --> 00:20:38,210
My...

314
00:20:38,460 --> 00:20:39,670
Besides that...

315
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:43,130
Please have a proper talk with Uncle Alberto.

316
00:20:43,210 --> 00:20:45,170
Until then, I won't speak to you, Father!

317
00:20:45,250 --> 00:20:50,040
Wh-What?! Please don't say that, Ellen!

318
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:54,290
Oh, I can't win against my daughter.

319
00:20:54,380 --> 00:20:59,170
It's hard to believe that Lady Ellen
is so keen at her age.

320
00:20:59,250 --> 00:21:01,290
I was deeply touched.

321
00:21:01,540 --> 00:21:04,130
Roren... Whose side are you on, anyway?

322
00:21:04,330 --> 00:21:06,630
Lady Ellen's, of course.

323
00:21:06,710 --> 00:21:08,170
Figures.

324
00:21:08,250 --> 00:21:11,960
I presume you understood
what she was trying to tell you.

325
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:15,750
Yeah. The reason Ellen burned
the letter without reading it

326
00:21:15,830 --> 00:21:20,210
was to prevent leaving any evidence
of Alberto's connection to Ravisel.

327
00:21:20,290 --> 00:21:24,500
Without that, there's no proof.
She saved Alberto.

328
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:26,080
Phenomenally done.

329
00:21:26,170 --> 00:21:28,210
Goodness, just who does she get it from?

330
00:21:28,290 --> 00:21:30,250
What are you saying?

331
00:21:30,330 --> 00:21:33,960
Lady Ellen is the spitting image
of you, my lord.

332
00:21:35,290 --> 00:21:37,130
That's the problem.

333
00:21:41,080 --> 00:21:43,710
You say she burned my letter
without reading it?

334
00:21:43,790 --> 00:21:44,830
Yes.

335
00:21:47,330 --> 00:21:49,960
As I have stated, this will be our last meeting.

336
00:21:50,380 --> 00:21:52,000
If you'll excuse me.

337
00:21:54,330 --> 00:22:00,920
She guessed my intentions and came back
with an even more surprising response.

338
00:22:01,580 --> 00:22:05,920
Reminds me of how I used
to interact with Rovel.

339
00:22:07,250 --> 00:22:09,960
I want her even more now.

340
00:22:10,080 --> 00:22:15,880
She's the key to solving the mystery of why the
royal family cannot form pacts with spirits.

341
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:20,040
Of that much I am sure.

342
00:22:21,170 --> 00:22:24,630
TRANSLATION: YUKARI MURASE-LOUDEN

343
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:28,330
EDITING: RILEY DALTON

344
00:22:28,670 --> 00:22:31,790
QUALITY CHECK: ASHLEY BARBOZA
